Package: microjs8
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: W5DMH <w5dmh@example.invalid>
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/W5DMH/microjs8
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-pil,
 python3-numpy,
 python3-evdev,
 python3-serial,
 python3-pip,
 libportaudio2,
 chrony,
 fonts-dejavu-core,
 adduser,
 systemd-sysv
Recommends: libhamlib-utils,
 gpsd,
 gpsd-clients
Description: MicroJS8 — JS8 transceiver for Raspberry Pi
 A self-contained JS8 transceiver daemon targeting the Raspberry Pi
 platform. Supports two host configurations:
   - M5Stack CardputerZero (on-board TCA8418 keyboard, ST7789 display)
   - Bare Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W with 1.9" ST7789V/V2 display
     (Waveshare or compatible) + USB keyboard
 Provides receive-decode-display, directed messaging, mailbox,
 emergency beacon, group calls, heartbeat broadcasts, and TX
 scheduling on the 320x170 panel.
 .
 Drives the radio via hamlib's rigctld (TS-480 emulation for QDX,
 G90 driver for Xiegu, RTS-PTT for DigiRig). Audio capture and
 playback go through PortAudio (libportaudio2) via the sounddevice
 Python module, which the postinst pip-installs since Debian does
 not currently package python3-sounddevice for Bookworm.
 .
 Installs to /usr/share/APPLaunch/ and registers as an APPLaunch
 application; the M5Stack launcher menu shows it as a tile on the
 CardputerZero, while bare Pi installs invoke it via the systemd
 service or directly via the microjs8 launcher script. A symlink
 at /usr/local/bin/microjs8-doctor exposes the diagnostic flag for
 convenient invocation.
